    "## 1 - Temperature\n",
    "\n",
    "We will group the temperature data by city and year to calculate central tendency and variability. These metrics help us understand how consistent or extreme the weather was in each city.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "1. Group the temperature data by `city name` and `year`\n",
    "2. Calculate the following statistics:\n",
    "   - Mean of average daily temperatures\n",
    "   - Standard deviation of average daily temperatures\n",
    "   - Maximum and minimum temperature recorded that year\n",
    "   - Annual temperature range (max - min)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute daily average temperature\n",
    "city_temperature_data['temperature avg'] = (\n",
    "    city_temperature_data['temperature max'] + city_temperature_data['temperature min']\n",
    ") / 2"
   ]
