    "## 5 – Interaction Term: Mean Temp × Temperature Variability\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, we test whether combining two climate features (mean temperature and its standard deviation) can help uncover any hidden patterns in the data that weren’t visible in our earlier visualizations.\n",
    "\n",
    "By creating a new feature (`mean temp × std dev temp`), we aim to explore whether temperature variability might interact with the baseline climate to influence mental health outcomes. This type of interaction can help reveal nonlinear relationships that are not captured when examining each feature separately.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "1. Create a new column: `interaction_term = mean temp × std dev temp`\n",
    "2. Plot a scatterplot of:\n",
    "   - x-axis: `interaction_term`\n",
    "   - y-axis: `mental distress %`\n",
    "   - hue: `year`\n",
    "3. Interpret any visible patterns or trends."
